{
  "id": "Compound::DB00493 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Cefotaxime, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is linked to Slc22a11 through a series of biological pathways that involve transport mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Cefotaxime, as part of the cephalosporin class, binds to Slc22a8, which is involved in the transport of organic cations and anions. This transport process is ultimately mediated by Slc22a11, indicating a potential role in the cellular uptake of cefotaxime. The shared ancestry of Cefotaxime with other cephalosporins and their common interaction with Slc22a11 underscores a broader mechanism of antibiotic transport and cellular uptake. The integration of these pathways highlights a dependency on Slc22a11 for the effective delivery of cephalosporins, suggesting that the transport of these antibiotics is governed by a conserved molecular mechanism involving the Slc22 family of transporters.",
